overview.problemStatement:
**δ(a,b)** is the highest bit position at which the binary expansions of distinct a,b differ — equivalently the most significant set bit of `a XOR b`. The stepping-up lemma needs:

- **(A) winner bit:** if a < b then at bit δ(a,b) the larger b has a 1 and a has a 0;
- **(B) distinctness:** for a < b < c, δ(a,b) ≠ δ(b,c);
- **(C) max law:** for a < b < c, δ(a,c) = max(δ(a,b), δ(b,c)).

All three are formalized here (0-axiom), with δ captured as a relation `TopDiff a b i` to stay fully constructive.
